  "summary": "The Napoleonic Wars continued the Wars of the French Revolution, as Britain and France fought for European supremacy. The Peace of Amiens of 1802 paused the fighting, but Britain declared war on France again in 1803. The wars ended with his defeat at Waterloo on 18 June 1815 by a coalition led by Wellington and Blücher.",
